\section{Renamed result tables and fields}{

Results use \code{logs} and \code{trees}, replacing \code{pieces} and \code{stems}. The old
\code{table} argument labels are translated by \code{\link[=product_summary]{product_summary()}} with a
message. Product construction translates \code{min_top_length} to
\code{min_boundary_length}, \code{continue_to_top} to \code{allow_lower_products}, and
\code{max_pieces} to \code{max_logs_per_segment}.

Supplying both old and new names
is an error. \code{scale_rule = 'exact_profile'} becomes \code{'cubic'} in
\code{\link[=product]{product()}}. These translations do not rename columns in an arbitrary
imported data frame.

Use current field names when importing tables.
}

\section{Measurement migration}{

Representable legacy \code{sold_by} values and expanded measurement fields
migrate with a deprecation message. The following table also applies to
\code{scale_rule}, \code{measurement_quantity}, \code{scale_unit}, and \code{scale_bark_basis}
combinations with the same meaning.\tabular{ll}{
   Legacy measurement \tab New fields or disposition \cr
   \code{scribner_decimal_c_whole_40}, \code{scribner_whole} \tab \code{scribner}, \code{split_scale = FALSE} \cr
   \code{scribner_decimal_c_split_20}, \code{scribner_split} \tab \code{scribner}, \code{split_scale = TRUE} \cr
   \code{international_1_4_4ft}, \code{international} \tab \code{volume_unit = 'international'} \cr
   \code{doyle_formula}, \code{doyle} \tab \code{volume_unit = 'doyle'} \cr
   \code{cubic_ft_ib}, \code{cubic_ft_ob}, \code{cubic_m_ib}, \code{cubic_m_ob} \tab \code{cubic}, matching bark and units \cr
   \code{green_short_ton}, \code{green_metric_ton} \tab \code{volume_unit = 'green_ton'}, matching call units \cr
   \code{cord_ib}, \code{cord_ob}, \code{cord} \tab \code{volume_unit = 'cord'}, matching bark \cr
   \code{cubic}, \code{green_ton} aliases \tab Same \code{volume_unit}, units follow the call \cr
   Smalian, Huber, factor Scribner, retired allocation \tab Stop, cannot express the procedure \cr
   Independent acceptance and cubic or cord bark bases \tab Stop, cannot express the combination \cr
   Custom rounding without an exact field equivalent \tab Stop, cannot express the override \cr
   Cubic or weight units opposite to the call units \tab Stop, cannot express the fixed unit \cr
}


\code{diameter_basis = 'ib'} becomes \code{inside_bark = TRUE}, and \code{'ob'} becomes \code{FALSE}. Board-foot
and green-weight measurements use inside bark. Cubic and cord measurements must match
acceptance bark.

Fixed legacy units survive construction, validation, and combination and are checked against
the merchandising call. The other defaults are \code{split_scale = FALSE} and \code{round = 'default'}. Expanded board-foot diameter rounding \code{rule_default}, \code{truncate_1in},
\code{nearest_1in_half_up}, and \code{none} maps to \code{default}, \code{down}, \code{nearest}, and \code{none}.

Other diameter operators and custom length or volume rounding are rejected.

Rejection names the setting, says the product fields cannot express it, and
points to the advanced reporting argument \code{report_also} for measurement forms
still available there. Named reporting definitions retain Smalian, Huber,
factor Scribner, fixed units, independent bark bases, and supported rounding
operators. The retired allocation is unavailable there. Reporting measures
existing cuts and does not change product acceptance or log selection.
}

